{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>יִרְאוּ</b> — R. Moses said: it should have been יִרְאוּ like קָרְאוּ, but the kamatz gadol comes unusually, so that it not be confused with יִרְאוּ (they fear) as in 'the righteous fear.' The meaning of 'His holy ones' — they are those who abandon the desires of the world and its pursuits. And the meaning of 'taste' (תִּרְאוּ) — that you not fear lest harm or lack come to them, even of their strength."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:28.509277298Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}